@module diagnostic
@lang aria
@version 0.1.0
@code_version git:fdea707
@aid_status reviewed
@aid_generated_by claude-opus-4-7
@aid_reviewed_by claude-opus-4-7
@layer 2
@aid_version 0.2
@purpose Compile-time error + warning reporting. Collects diagnostics from every phase (lexer / parser / resolver / checker) with source positions, severity levels, and formatted output (text or JSON). Does not halt on first error — phases emit what they can and the driver decides when to stop.
@depends []

---

@workflow accumulate_and_report
@purpose How a diagnostic flows from a phase to the user
@steps
  1. Phase builds a Diagnostic via new_error() / new_warning() with code + message + Span. [src: diagnostic.aria:137-141]
  2. bag_add_diagnostic() dedupes on (code, line, file), increments counters, appends to bag. [src: diagnostic.aria:165-190]
  3. Phases merge bags via bag_merge() to aggregate errors across compilation stages. [src: diagnostic.aria:204-212]
  4. Driver polls bag_has_errors() to decide whether to halt; renders via render_text() or render_json_bag(). [src: diagnostic.aria:399-554]

@workflow text_rendering
@purpose Diagnostic -> human-readable output
@steps
  1. render_text() prefixes "severity[code]: message" + span location. [src: diagnostic.aria:399-403]
  2. _get_source_line() extracts the relevant source line; line-number width computed for gutter alignment. [src: diagnostic.aria:374-389]
  3. Source line emitted with caret underline beneath the error position. [src: diagnostic.aria:405-422]
  4. Notes appended at the end. [src: diagnostic.aria:424-432]

---

@invariants
  Sentinel element at DiagnosticBag index 0 is a placeholder; real diagnostics start at index 1. [src: diagnostic.aria:158-163, diagnostic.aria:206]
  Deduplication key is (code, line, file). Later duplicates are silently dropped — useful for phases that re-emit the same error across lines. [src: diagnostic.aria:166-174]
  Severity enum values map to hardcoded strings for output stability. [src: diagnostic.aria:16-21]
  Error / warning code constants (E0001..E0704, W0001..W0100) are immutable strings with 1:1 mapping via describe_code. [src: diagnostic.aria:222-358]
  Span fields (line, col, offset, length) are i64; rendering assumes 1-based line + col. [src: diagnostic.aria:49-81]

---

@antipatterns
  Appending directly to DiagnosticBag.diagnostics bypasses dedup and counter updates. Always go through bag_add_* or new_*. [src: diagnostic.aria:137-148, diagnostic.aria:158-163]
  Span length < 1 is silently clamped to a 1-character underline during rendering — no signal to the caller that the span was malformed. [src: diagnostic.aria:414-418]
  JSON rendering filters empty label/suggestion messages while text rendering shows everything: output parity between formats is not a given. [src: diagnostic.aria:494-507, diagnostic.aria:514-526]
  Large bags degrade: bag_add_diagnostic is O(n) per add (linear dedup scan); bag_merge is O(m*n). Avoid merging many large bags repeatedly. [src: diagnostic.aria:167-174, diagnostic.aria:207-209]

---

@fn new_bag
@purpose Initialize an empty DiagnosticBag with a sentinel at index 0 and zeroed counts.
@post DiagnosticBag with diagnostics=[sentinel], error_count=0, warning_count=0. [src: diagnostic.aria:158-163]
@complexity O(1).
@thread_safety immutable — fresh allocation.

---

@fn bag_add_diagnostic
@purpose Add a Diagnostic to the bag with dedup + counter update.
@post New bag with diag appended (or skipped if duplicate); counter incremented only on fresh adds. [src: diagnostic.aria:175-189]
@complexity O(n) linear dedup scan (n = current bag size). [src: diagnostic.aria:167-174]
@thread_safety immutable — functional update.

---

@fn bag_add_error / bag_add_warning
@purpose One-shot constructors that build the Diagnostic then call bag_add_diagnostic.
@complexity O(n) dedup cost. [src: diagnostic.aria:192-196]
@antipatterns No code-format validation — a typoed code like "E01" is accepted silently. [src: diagnostic.aria:192, diagnostic.aria:195]

---

@fn bag_has_errors
@purpose Predicate — true iff bag.error_count > 0.
@complexity O(1) field access. [src: diagnostic.aria:198]
@antipatterns Does not consider Warning/Info/Hint. Callers that want to fail on warnings must check warning_count separately. [src: diagnostic.aria:198]

---

@fn bag_merge
@purpose Combine two bags, preserving counts and deduping.
@complexity O(m*n) — nested loop dedup. Avoid on hot paths. [src: diagnostic.aria:204-212]
@thread_safety immutable — returns a new bag.

---

@fn new_error / new_warning
@purpose Construct a Diagnostic at Error / Warning severity.
@post Returns Diagnostic with severity set, primary label, and empty suggestion defaults. [src: diagnostic.aria:132-141]
@antipatterns Initializes with a placeholder label and empty suggestion. Callers often need to filter or overwrite these before rendering. [src: diagnostic.aria:132-135]

---

@fn diag_with_note
@purpose Attach an educational note string to an existing Diagnostic.
@complexity O(notes.len()) amortized (array copy on append). [src: diagnostic.aria:143-145]
@antipatterns No note dedup. Empty notes from init (line 133) can accumulate — filter manually. [src: diagnostic.aria:133, diagnostic.aria:143-145]

---

@fn render_text
@purpose Format a single Diagnostic as human text with source context + caret underline + notes.
@pre source is the full source file text (newline-delimited); diag references positions within it. [src: diagnostic.aria:399]
@complexity O(source.len()) to split and extract the offending line; O(span.col) for the underline. [src: diagnostic.aria:374-422]
@antipatterns _get_source_line re-splits the source on every call. When rendering many diagnostics from the same source, cache the split. [src: diagnostic.aria:374-380]

---

@fn render_json_diagnostic
@purpose Serialize a single Diagnostic to JSON with code / severity / message / span / labels / suggestions.
@pre String fields must not contain unescaped quotes or backslashes — caller's responsibility. [src: diagnostic.aria:468]
@complexity O(message.len() + labels + suggestions). [src: diagnostic.aria:468-530]
@antipatterns Filters empty label/suggestion messages, so JSON output is a strict subset of text output — downstream consumers that expect parity will miss fields. [src: diagnostic.aria:494-507, diagnostic.aria:514-526]

---

@fn render_json_bag
@purpose Serialize an entire DiagnosticBag with a summary block of error + warning counts.
@complexity O(D * L) — D diagnostics, L avg labels + suggestions. [src: diagnostic.aria:532-554]
@antipatterns Skips the index-0 sentinel; any direct array manipulation that moves the sentinel breaks this. [src: diagnostic.aria:538-539]

